    "README.md": "# Helpers\n\nUtilities.\n\n## Functions\n\n### numbers.total(values)\n\n- Ignores `None` values.\n- Keeps zero and negative numbers.\n- Returns `0` for empty input or when all items are `None`.\n\nExamples:\n\n```python\nfrom numbers import total\n\ntotal([2, None, -1, 0])  # 1\ntotal([None])            # 0\ntotal([])                # 0\n```\n\n### labels.normalize(value)\n\n- Strips leading and trailing whitespace.\n- Converts to lowercase.\n- Preserves internal spaces.\n\nExamples:\n\n```python\nfrom labels import normalize\n\nnormalize(\" A B \")  # \"a b\"\nnormalize(\"  \")     # \"\"\n```\n",
    "test_numbers.py": "import unittest\nfrom numbers import total\n\nclass NumbersTest(unittest.TestCase):\n    def test_total(self):\n        self.assertEqual(total([2, None, -1, 0]), 1)\n    def test_empty(self):\n        self.assertEqual(total([None]), 0)\n",
    "test_labels.py": "import unittest\nfrom labels import normalize\n\nclass LabelsTest(unittest.TestCase):\n    def test_normalize(self):\n        self.assertEqual(normalize(' A B '), 'a b')\n    def test_empty(self):\n        self.assertEqual(normalize('  '), '')\n"
